<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland announces winners of Rockall oil licences.</title>
<headline>Ireland announces winners of Rockall oil licences.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland on Wednesday announced the successful applicants for exploration licences to prospect for oil in the Rockall Trough off the Irish west coast.</p>
<p>Ireland's minister of state at the Department of Energy, Emmet Stagg said he had decided that 11 explorateion licences should be granted covering 58 full and part blocks.  </p>
<p>The licence awards in alphabetical order are as follows:</p>
<p>-- Arco, BG and Anadarko are being awarded a three block licence over blocks 18/9, 18/10 and 19/6. -- BG, Arco and Anadarko are being awarded a four full and two half block licences over blocks 16/27, the southern half of 25/1, 25/2, 25/6 and the eastern half of 75/9 and 75/10.</p>
</text>
